age of RCC is chromophobe?","a":["4%-5%."],"topic":"RCC histology","priority":"Core","marks":1,"subtopics":["rcc-pathology"]},{"id":"rt-d17","q":"What percentage is unclassified RCC?","a":["1%-5%."],"topic":"RCC histology","priority":"Core","marks":1,"subtopics":["rcc-pathology"]},{"id":"rt-d18","q":"What is notable about collecting duct carcinoma?","a":["It is rare and has a poor prognosis."],"topic":"RCC histology","priority":"Core","marks":2,"subtopics":["rcc-pathology"]},{"id":"rt-d19","q":"What is notable about renal medullary carcinoma?","a":["It is uncommon and occurs almost exclusively in patients with sickle cell trait."],"topic":"RCC histology","priority":"High","marks":2,"subtopics":["rcc-pathology"]},{"id":"rt-d20","q":"How is RCC usually discovered?","a":["Incidentally."],"topic":"RCC diagnosis","priority":"High","marks":1,"subtopics":["rcc-clinical"]},{"id":"rt-d21","q":"What does the complete RCC triad correlate with?","a":["Aggressive histology and advanced disease."],"topic":"RCC diagnosis","priority":"High","marks":2,"subtopics":["rcc-clinical"]},{"id":"rt-d22","q":"Why may a non-reducible varicocele occur in RCC?","a":["Obstruction of the testicular vein."],"topic":"RCC examination","priority":"Core","marks":2,"subtopics":["rcc-clinical"]},{"id":"rt-d23","q":"Which supraclavicular node may be found in RCC?","a":["The left supraclavicular node, or Virchow gland."],"topic":"RCC examination","priority":"Core","marks":2,"subtopics":["rcc-clinical"]},{"id":"rt-d24","q":"What may CBC show in RCC?","a":["Anemia or polycythemia."],"topic":"RCC investigations","priority":"Core","marks":2,"subtopics":["rcc-investigations"]},{"id":"rt-d25","q":"What may urinalysis show in RCC?","a":["Hematuria."],"topic":"RCC investigations","priority":"Core","marks":1,"subtopics":["rcc-investigations"]},{"id":"rt-d26","q":"What may ultrasound show in RCC?","a":["A solid or partially cystic mass."],"topic":"RCC imaging","priority":"Core","marks":2,"subtopics":["rcc-investigations"]},{"id":"rt-d27","q":"What is the main benefit of MRI stated for RCC?","a":["Diagnosis and staging without ionizing radiation."],"topic":"RCC imaging","priority":"Core","marks":2,"subtopics":["rcc-investigations"]},{"id":"rt-d28","q":"For which renal tumor is partial nephrectomy stated?","a":["A small renal tumor."],"topic":"RCC treatment","priority":"High","marks":1,"subtopics":["rcc-treatment"]},{"id":"rt-d29","q":"For which renal tumor is radical nephrectomy stated?","a":["A larger renal tumor."],"topic":"RCC treatment","priority":"High","marks":1,"subtopics":["rcc-treatment"]},{"id":"rt-d30","q":"What is the usual age stated for Wilms tumor?","a":["4 years."],"topic":"Wilms pathology","priority":"High","marks":1,"subtopics":["wilms-pathology"]},{"id":"rt-d31","q":"From what tissue does Wilms tumor arise?","a":["Embryonic nephrogenic tissue."],"topic":"Wilms pathology","priority":"High","marks":2,"subtopics":["wilms-pathology"]},{"id":"rt-d32","q":"Describe the gross appearance of Wilms tumor.","a":["Large, multilobulated and gray."],"topic":"Wilms pathology","priority":"Core","marks":2,"subtopics":["wilms-pathology"]},{"id":"rt-d33","q":"How is Wilms histology broadly classified?","a":["Favorable or unfavorable histology."],"topic":"Wilms pathology","priority":"Core","marks":2,"subtopics":["wilms-pathology"]},{"id":"rt-d34","q":"Who often discovers the abdominal mass in Wilms tumor?","a":["The mother or the doctor."],"topic":"Wilms clinical","priority":"Core","marks":1,"subtopics":["wilms-clinical"]},{"id":"rt-d35","q":"What causes hypertension in Wilms tumor according to the lecture?","a":["Renin production."],"topic":"Wilms clinical","priority":"High","marks":2,"subtopics":["wilms-clinical"]},{"id":"rt-d36","q":"What is the primary investigation of choice in Wilms tumor?","a":["Ultrasound."],"topic":"Wilms investigations","priority":"High","marks":1,"subtopics":["wilms-investigations"]},{"id":"rt-d37","q":"Why is MRI favored in Wilms tumor?","a":["It avoids ionizing radiation."],"topic":"Wilms investigations","priority":"High","marks":2,"subtopics":["wilms-investigations"]},{"id":"rt-d38","q":"What survival rate is stated for Wilms tumor?","a":["Up to 90%."],"topic":"Wilms prognosis","priority":"Core","marks":1,"subtopics":["wilms-treatment"]},{"id":"rt-d39","q":"What proportion of urothelial tumors are UTUCs?","a":["5%-10%."],"topic":"UTUC epidemiology","priority":"High","marks":1,"subtopics":["utuc-epidemiology-risk"]},{"id":"rt-d40","q":"What proportion of UTUC patients may have bilateral disease?","a":["Up to 5%."],"topic":"UTUC epidemiology","priority":"Core","marks":1,"subtopics":["utuc-epidemiology-risk"]},{"id":"rt-d41","q":"How often is concurrent bladder cancer diagnosed in UTUC?","a":["17% of cases."],"topic":"UTUC epidemiology","priority":"Core","marks":1,"subtopics":["utuc-epidemiology-risk"]},{"id":"rt-d42","q":"Where do upper tract urothelial carcinomas arise?","a":["In the lining of the renal pelvis or ureter."],"topic":"UTUC pathology","priority":"High","marks":2,"subtopics":["utuc-pathology-diagnosis"]},{"id":"rt-d43","q":"What percentage of upper urinary tract tumors are urothelial carcinomas?","a":["About 90%."],"topic":"UTUC pathology","priority":"High","marks":1,"subtopics":["utuc-pathology-diagnosis"]},{"id":"rt-d44","q":"What symptoms characterize localized UTUC?","a":["Hematuria, dysuria and flank pain."],"topic":"UTUC diagnosis","priority":"High","marks":3,"subtopics":["utuc-pathology-diagnosis"]},{"id":"rt-d45","q":"What symptoms characterize advanced UTUC?","a":["Flank or abdominal mass, weight loss, anorexia and bone pain."],"topic":"UTUC diagnosis","priority":"Core","marks":4,"subtopics":["utuc-pathology-diagnosis"]}],"rapid":[["RCC is usually discovered how?","Incidentally."],["Peak RCC age?","60-70 years."],["RCC male:female ratio?","3:2."],["Three lifestyle RCC risks?","Smoking, obesity and hypertension."],["VHL chromosome?","3p."],["RCC cell of origin?","Renal tubular epithelial cells."],["Why is RCC yellow?","High fat content."],["Most common RCC subtype?","Clear cell, 70%-80%."],["RCC subtype linked to sickle cell trait?","Renal medullary carcinoma."],["Classic RCC triad?","Flank pain, painless gross hematuria and palpable mass."],["RCC varicocele mechanism?","Testicular vein obstruction."],["Contrast CT role in RCC?","Diagnosis and staging."],["Small renal tumor operation?","Partial nephrectomy."],["Larger renal tumor operation?","Radical nephrectomy."],["Wilms usual age in the lecture?","4 years."],["Wilms tissue of origin?","Embryonic nephrogenic tissue."],["Wilms gross appearance?","Large, multilobulated and gray."],["Wilms hypertension mechanism?","Renin production."],["Primary Wilms imaging?","Ultrasound."],["Wilms treatment triad?","Nephrectomy, chemotherapy and radiotherapy."],["Wilms survival stated?","Up to 90%."],["UTUC share of urothelial tumors?","5%-10%."],["UTUC bilateral disease?","Up to 5%."],["Concurrent bladder cancer with UTUC?","17%."],["Hereditary UTUC syndrome?","Lynch syndrome (HNPCC)."],["Tobacco relative risk for UTUC?","2.5-7 times."],["Best diagnostic imaging for UTUC?","CT urography."],["Key endoscopic diagnostic approach?","Flexible ureteroscopy with biopsy."],["Goblet sign suggests?","Ureteral urothelial/TCC tumor."],["Definitive UTUC operation?","Nephroureterectomy with bladder cuff removal."]]}